Cancer: An Overview

Garima Mathur, Sumitra Nain and Pramod Kumar Sharma

1 School of Medical and Allied Sciences, Galgotia university, Greater Noida, India 2 Department of Pharmacy, Banasthali University, Banasthali, Rajasthan-304022, India

Abstract: Now a day’s cancer is the most prevalent life threatening disease which is spreading because of the lifestyle we are living. Cancer is due to uncontrolled growth of cell which can be cured if diagnosed in early stage of life. Treatment of cancer depends on the various internal and external factors causing cancer. Cancer is screened by different screening test and a number of treatments are now available these days such as gene therapy, chemotherapy, surgery, radiation therapy, immunotherapy etc. In future up to 2030 around 22.2 million cases are expected to be diagnosed for cancer.

